n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1-(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537881 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537881 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96306" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537881 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537881 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int ({cosh}^{3}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537881 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "032608f7-6edc-5183-bb2d-4ede3e9c1645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537881 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cosh}^{3}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x({cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537890 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537890 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537890 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537890 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int (2{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{x}^{3}-2{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537890 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c959d7c-d68c-591a-a3b7-ea71063de12e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537890 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{x}^{3}-2{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2[{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]+4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2+4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\cdot \\text{d}x+\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x+{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537900 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537900 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165872" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537900 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537900 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537900 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "347de47e-5245-5fd2-b46a-2d80ee9ca643" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537900 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537902 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537902 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96435" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537902 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537902 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-1}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537902 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "36b4a778-aa5a-54d9-9b61-eb9431bef188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537902 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-1={csch}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-1}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{({coth}^{2}⁡x-1)({coth}^{2}⁡x+1)}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({coth}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{17}{15}+\\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{60}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537912 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537912 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96413" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537912 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537912 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537912 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e26e540-b6e1-55b9-88da-a99de2917513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537912 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{sech}^{2}⁡x={tanh}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{3}^{2}+1}{{3}^{2}-1}+\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537915 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537915 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165894" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537915 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537915 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{2+2{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537915 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "56c765b2-a04b-54c3-b2ad-79e20147ade9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537915 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x) & =1 \\\\ 1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x) & ={cosh}^{2}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2+2{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x))}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537925 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537925 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96307" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537925 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537925 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537925 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6bf4783e-de85-5ad3-95bc-1eadaee336f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537925 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537926 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537926 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96405" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537926 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537926 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537926 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6c61796b-b24c-5403-8a9e-cd8bda63e7c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537926 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡(1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537928 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537928 #edb/ref 1069 "q-362032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537928 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537928 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537928 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "70e33acb-bebf-51b2-9607-6c52a3430a18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537928 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{2}^{7} \\\\  & =7-2 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537929 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537929 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537929 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537929 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537929 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7461b1f3-1aea-5d09-ab06-c9f25cb75e4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537929 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot (1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡0) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}+{e}^{-(0)}}{2}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{2+{2}^{-1}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{5}{4}-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537930 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537930 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537930 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537930 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537930 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7649fd25-c8c5-5938-a768-41b9d4f9aa06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537930 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =2x-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1) & =1 \\\\ {cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1) & =1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537943 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537943 #edb/ref 1069 "q-347992" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537943 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537943 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537943 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9ddcb9f3-50a1-505b-ae57-c8a55dc1f652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537943 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{sech}^{2}⁡x={tanh}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+{2}^{-1}}{2-{2}^{-1}}-\\frac{4+{4}^{-1}}{4-{4}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{17}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537944 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537944 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537944 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537944 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+{csch}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537944 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9ea30f92-f367-5355-89e8-50b8c17d0449" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537944 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1+{csch}^{2}⁡x={coth}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+{csch}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(1+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {coth}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2-{2}^{-1}}-\\frac{2}{3-{3}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537949 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537949 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96429" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537949 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537949 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a49f44d3-1abb-5067-966c-70ae50d2155e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537949 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{1-{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}-2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{0}-1}{{e}^{0}+1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}-1}{{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537967 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537967 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165895" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537967 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537967 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{6}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537967 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7a3ee0b-1bd5-5d07-b45d-54312bc57611" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537967 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =3x+2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2) & =1 \\\\ 1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2) & ={cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {sech}^{2}⁡(3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348041" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537975 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537975 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1+{csch}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d50512b3-2d0b-53b0-a169-ed8ad3f44908" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537975 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1+{csch}^{2}⁡x={coth}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1+{csch}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡8)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-{8}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{2-{2}^{-1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{16}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{51}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537985 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537985 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96522" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537985 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537985 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{csch}^{3}⁡(7x-2)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537985 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f321e82d-23c7-5f15-828b-dbb232e439d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537985 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={csch}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =7x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-1 & ={csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2) \\\\ {coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2) & ={csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{csch}^{3}⁡(7x-2)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)[{csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2)+1]}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2){coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537991 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186537760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537991 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348060" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537991 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537991 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537991 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe6b40d3-8971-55c8-aabc-4ac03f347ec4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537991 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
